====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The position of a [[person]] or [[team]] in a [[tournament]] or [[competition]] who [[draw]]s no [[opponent]] in a [[particular]] [[round]] so [[advance]]s to the next round [[unopposed]], or is awarded [[points]] for a [[win]] in a [[league table]]; also the [[phantom]] opponent of such a person or team.
#: {{ux|en|Craig's Crew plays the '''bye''' next week.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020| title=From Darkness to Dynasty|author=Jerry Thornton | page=| passage=The Patriots were in the unique situation of having to play 16 straight games, then have their '''bye''' in week 17, whether they needed it or not.}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} An [[extra]] scored when the [[batsman|batsmen]] take [[run]]s after the [[ball]] has passed the [[striker]] without hitting [[either]] the [[bat]] or the batsman.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A thing not directly aimed at; a secondary or subsidiary object, course, path, undertaking, issue, etc.
#* {{RQ:Fuller Church History
|passage=The Synod of Dort in some points condemneth, upon the '''by''', even the discipline of the Church of England.}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} An unspecified way or place.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1815| title=Guy Manneringv|author=Sir Walter Scott| passage=Frank Kennedy will shew you the penalties in the act, and ye ken yoursell they used to put their run goods into the auld Place of Ellangowan up '''bye''' there.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1880| title=Johnny Gibb|author=W. Alexander| page=| passage=This was lattin at me, ye ken, for inveetin the coachman an' the gamekeeper up '''bye'''. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year= 1894| title=Margridel|author=David Storrar Meldrum| page=| passage=No word of a new house-keeper down '''bye''', Wull?}}
#* {{RQ:Buchan Witch Wood| passage=There's a friend of yours up '''bye''' that would be blithe to see you—up the rig from the auld aik on the road to the Greenshiel. }}
# {{lb|en|card games}} A [[pass]].

